      "solution": [
        "acl-author {\"kind\":\"ApplyDocuments\",\"documents\":{\"schema_version\":1,\"routers\":{\"Gateway\":\"ip access-list extended services\\n 20 permit udp any any eq 53\\n 10 permit tcp any any eq 443\\nexit\\ninterface office\\n ip access-group services in\\nexit\\n\"}}}"
      ],
      "prerequisites": [],
      "acl_teaching": {
        "prerequisite_note": "Assumes IPv4 host addresses and the purpose of TCP/UDP ports. This introduction explains rule order, wildcard address matching and where an ACL is applied. You may skip it or reopen it later.",
        "concepts": [
          {
            "title": "Allow the listed service flows",
            "text": "A rule permits or denies matching packets. TCP 443 and UDP 53 name the virtual HTTPS and DNS flows in this task; no real service is contacted. Rules run in order and the first match wins. A populated ACL denies unmatched packets, while an interface with no ACL does not filter here."
          },
          {
            "title": "Match addresses and ports explicitly",
            "text": "any matches all addresses. host ADDRESS matches one address. In ADDRESS WILDCARD, a zero bit must match and a one bit is ignored; a wildcard is not a prefix mask. TCP and UDP rows can match destination ports with eq NUMBER; source-port conditions are a different position."
          },
          {
            "title": "Apply a policy at a virtual boundary",
            "text": "interface office selects the supplied virtual diagram label, not a physical IOS port inventory. ip access-group NAME in checks incoming transit traffic before routing. Edit the complete router document; applying replaces its ACLs and bindings. Omitted sections clear them. This bounded native editor is not a full IOS command session."
          }
        ],
        "example_description": "In this isolated example, DemoPC 203.0.113.10 needs TCP 8080 on DemoService 10.20.0.20, while TCP 23 must be blocked at DemoGateway/office input. Fill worked example edits only this example draft; apply/check explicitly. Assignment values and work are separate.",
